CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to complaint handling;
b. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
c. the right to receive protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on protection orders from the court;
d. the right to health and psychological recovery from suffering experienced by victims;
e. the right to determine their own decisions;
f. the right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. the right to obtain information;
h. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; and
k. the right to spiritual guidance services.

Part Five

Handling of Women and Children Victims of Violence Article 36

The implementation of handling of women and children victims of violence shall be carried out with:

a. speed;
b. safety and comfort;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. accessibility;
f. free of charge; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

Article 37

Forms of handling of women and children victims of violence include:

a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. assistance services;
c. medical rehabilitation services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services; and
f. social reintegration services.

Part Four

Prevention of Violence against Women and Children Article 34

(1) Efforts to prevent violence against women and children shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government and coordinated by the technical SKPD.

(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:

a. conducting guidance towards harmonious household integrity;
b. establishing a working network in efforts to prevent violence; c. carrying out coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
f. providing critical education regarding the rights of women and children to the community.

Article 39

Assistance services as referred to in Article 37 letter b include:

a. accompanying victims during examination and health recovery processes;
b. accompanying victims during examination processes at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
c. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in examination processes at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
d. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all unauthorized parties, including reporting by mass media; e. providing a sense of security to victims; and
f. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

Article 24

(1) The implementation of Protection and empowerment of children in the field of social welfare as referred to in Article 13 letter d, the Regional Government is obliged to organize social welfare for:

