CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to complaint handling;
b. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
c. the right to receive protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on protection orders from the court;
d. the right to health and psychological recovery from suffering experienced by victims;
e. the right to determine their own decisions;
f. the right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. the right to obtain information;
h. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; and
k. the right to spiritual guidance services.

Article 46

Women and children victims of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 45, shall also receive special rights, as follows:

a. the right to survival;
b. the right to grow and develop;
c. the right to receive equal protection; and d. the right to participate in community life.

