7.3.text:
CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to complaint handling;
b. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
c. the right to receive protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on protection orders from the court;
d. the right to health and psychological recovery from suffering experienced by victims;
e. the right to determine their own decisions;
f. the right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. the right to obtain information;
h. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
i. the right to social rehabilitation;
j. the right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; and
k. the right to spiritual guidance services.

Article 44

(1) The implementation of services for women and children victims of violence shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the PPT.

(2) The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes an integrated part and is unified with the PPT that implements integrated services for witnesses and/or victims of human trafficking crimes.

(3) The implementation of services for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. providing fast and free services to victims; b. implementing protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;

c. cooperating with certain institutions in providing translators and assisting volunteers needed for victims;

d. networking with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperating with witness and victim protection agencies, social protection homes or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for health recovery of victims;

e. providing convenience, comfort and safety for victims;

f. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; and

g. providing fulfillment of legal assistance for victims.

(4) Further provisions regarding procedures and mechanisms for implementing the PPT shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children; b. maintain the integrity of the household to realize a harmonious family;
c. prevent violence against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; e. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and g. carry out empowerment for women victims of violence.

